1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,697
Opening the box.

2
00:00:01,697 --> 00:00:03,550
Every file, explained.

3
00:00:04,350 --> 00:00:07,242
Wagtail start generated twenty nine files.

4
00:00:07,242 --> 00:00:11,993
Most tutorials explain three of them and tell you to ignore the rest.

5
00:00:11,993 --> 00:00:17,502
We are reading all of them, because the ones you are told to ignore are the ones

6
00:00:17,502 --> 00:00:20,256
deciding how your site actually behaves.

7
00:00:21,056 --> 00:00:22,846
And we change nothing.

8
00:00:22,846 --> 00:00:23,903
Not one line.

9
00:00:23,903 --> 00:00:29,435
Start from git checkout e p zero one end if you are following along.

10
00:00:29,435 --> 00:00:32,282
Read the box before you rebuild it.

11
00:00:33,082 --> 00:00:34,634
Start at manage.py.

12
00:00:34,634 --> 00:00:40,350
Standard Django, and one line matters: the settings module defaults to

13
00:00:40,350 --> 00:00:41,983
studio.settings.dev.

14
00:00:41,983 --> 00:00:43,453
That is the split.

15
00:00:43,453 --> 00:00:46,719
You get development settings by default,

16
00:00:46,719 --> 00:00:50,884
and production settings only when you ask for them.

17
00:00:51,684 --> 00:00:56,208
Then two path variables that look almost the same and are not.

18
00:00:56,208 --> 00:00:58,178
Project dir is the package.

19
00:00:58,178 --> 00:01:00,513
Base dir is the folder above it.

20
00:01:00,513 --> 00:01:06,205
They are one letter apart in your head and mixing them up is a classic bug two

21
00:01:06,205 --> 00:01:07,518
episodes from now.

22
00:01:08,318 --> 00:01:11,646
Now the file that matters most.

23
00:01:11,646 --> 00:01:13,256
Installed apps.

24
00:01:14,056 --> 00:01:16,941
This is the whole thesis of the series.

25
00:01:16,941 --> 00:01:20,345
Wagtail is not a black box bolted onto Django.

26
00:01:20,345 --> 00:01:24,857
It is eleven Django apps sitting in your installed apps list.

27
00:01:24,857 --> 00:01:30,850
Every one of them has models, and you can query them like any other Django model.

28
00:01:31,650 --> 00:01:36,276
Middleware is the standard Django stack plus exactly one addition,

29
00:01:36,276 --> 00:01:38,099
and it is last on purpose.

30
00:01:38,099 --> 00:01:43,286
The redirect middleware only acts once everything else has produced a 404,

31
00:01:43,286 --> 00:01:46,020
and then it checks the redirects table.

32
00:01:46,820 --> 00:01:50,328
Then four settings people mix up constantly.

33
00:01:50,328 --> 00:01:53,437
Static files dirs is where you put CSS.

34
00:01:53,437 --> 00:01:58,220
Static root is where collect static dumps it for production.

35
00:01:58,220 --> 00:02:00,851
Media root is where uploads land.

36
00:02:00,851 --> 00:02:06,113
The rule that keeps it straight: static is code, media is content.

37
00:02:06,113 --> 00:02:09,302
Static gets committed, media never does.

38
00:02:10,102 --> 00:02:13,187
And the Wagtail block at the bottom.

39
00:02:13,187 --> 00:02:19,184
Site name, the search backend, a ten megabyte cap on document uploads.

40
00:02:19,184 --> 00:02:22,183
But look at wagtail admin base url.

41
00:02:22,183 --> 00:02:24,840
It ships as http://example.com.

42
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:28,267
That is a placeholder that ships broken.

43
00:02:28,267 --> 00:02:33,494
It builds absolute URLs for notification emails and previews.

44
00:02:33,494 --> 00:02:36,064
We fix it in episode thirteen.

45
00:02:36,864 --> 00:02:39,332
The two settings files are tiny.

46
00:02:39,332 --> 00:02:45,810
Dev turns debug on and ships a secret key marked, in the variable name, as insecure.

47
00:02:45,810 --> 00:02:47,893
Production turns debug off.

48
00:02:47,893 --> 00:02:54,063
And both end with the same trick: a local.py file that does not exist and is not

49
00:02:54,063 --> 00:02:56,530
committed can override anything.

50
00:02:56,530 --> 00:03:00,618
That is the escape hatch for machine specific config.

51
00:03:01,418 --> 00:03:06,116
Now urls.py, and the order is the whole point.

52
00:03:06,916 --> 00:03:09,823
That last line is Wagtail's catch all.

53
00:03:09,823 --> 00:03:14,566
Any URL that did not match above gets handed to the page tree,

54
00:03:14,566 --> 00:03:17,244
which resolves it by walking slugs.

55
00:03:17,244 --> 00:03:23,516
That is why a page at/about/team just works and nobody wrote a URL pattern for it.

56
00:03:23,516 --> 00:03:26,653
And it is why this line has to stay last.

57
00:03:26,653 --> 00:03:30,478
Put a route after it and it will never be reached.

58
00:03:31,278 --> 00:03:32,442
The home app.

59
00:03:32,442 --> 00:03:38,530
models.py is six lines, and that is already a working CMS page type.

60
00:03:38,530 --> 00:03:45,335
Title, slug, SEO fields, publishing dates, revisions, previews, permissions.

61
00:03:45,335 --> 00:03:48,021
All of it inherited from Page.

62
00:03:48,021 --> 00:03:50,976
We add fields to it next episode.

63
00:03:51,776 --> 00:03:55,576
And notice the template naming convention.

64
00:03:55,576 --> 00:04:01,549
The model is called HomePage, so Wagtail looks for home_page.html.

65
00:04:01,549 --> 00:04:05,259
Model name, lowercased, with underscores.

66
00:04:05,259 --> 00:04:07,159
You never wire it up.

67
00:04:07,159 --> 00:04:09,602
Episode four exploits that.

68
00:04:10,402 --> 00:04:15,637
Now the centrepiece of this episode, and the file almost nobody opens.

69
00:04:15,637 --> 00:04:21,021
Your homepage was not a fixture, and you did not create it in the admin.

70
00:04:21,021 --> 00:04:25,284
A data migration made it, the first time you ran migrate.

71
00:04:25,284 --> 00:04:30,220
That is why a brand new Wagtail site already has exactly one page.

72
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:32,581
It does three things.

73
00:04:32,581 --> 00:04:36,448
It deletes the default page that wagtail core ships.

74
00:04:36,448 --> 00:04:38,976
It gets or creates a content type,

75
00:04:38,976 --> 00:04:43,586
which is how a single Page row knows which model it really is.

76
00:04:43,586 --> 00:04:48,270
And then it creates the page, with values that look like magic.

77
00:04:49,070 --> 00:04:52,921
Path equals zero zero zero one, zero zero zero one.

78
00:04:52,921 --> 00:04:56,773
That is a materialised path, from django treebeard,

79
00:04:56,773 --> 00:05:00,246
the package we watched install in episode one.

80
00:05:00,246 --> 00:05:02,210
Four characters per level.

81
00:05:02,210 --> 00:05:04,551
Zero zero zero one is the root.

82
00:05:04,551 --> 00:05:08,780
Its first child is that plus another zero zero zero one.

83
00:05:08,780 --> 00:05:10,668
Its child adds four more.

84
00:05:10,668 --> 00:05:14,066
The entire ancestry is encoded in the string,

85
00:05:14,066 --> 00:05:20,258
which is how Wagtail can fetch a page's parents in one query instead of walking up

86
00:05:20,258 --> 00:05:22,448
the tree one level at a time.

87
00:05:23,248 --> 00:05:28,857
Run that query on your own site and you will see something surprising: there are

88
00:05:28,857 --> 00:05:30,189
two pages, not one.

89
00:05:30,189 --> 00:05:33,484
There is an invisible Root above your homepage.

90
00:05:33,484 --> 00:05:37,690
That is why the admin shows your page nested one level down.

91
00:05:38,490 --> 00:05:42,646
And one last line in that migration creates a Site row.

92
00:05:42,646 --> 00:05:47,482
Hostname localhost, default site, root page set to our homepage.

93
00:05:47,482 --> 00:05:50,278
Wagtail is multi site out of the box,

94
00:05:50,278 --> 00:05:54,132
and this is the row that makes your one site exist.

95
00:05:54,932 --> 00:06:00,583
The search app is a plain Django function view, about thirty five lines,

96
00:06:00,583 --> 00:06:01,918
with a paginator.

97
00:06:01,918 --> 00:06:07,334
Note .live, which means published pages only, so drafts are excluded.

98
00:06:07,334 --> 00:06:11,337
It is wired up already, but nothing is indexed yet.

99
00:06:11,337 --> 00:06:13,142
That is episode eleven.

100
00:06:13,942 --> 00:06:18,085
base.html gives you an SEO title with a fallback for free,

101
00:06:18,085 --> 00:06:23,800
and the wagtail user bar, which is the floating admin bar that logged in editors

102
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:26,158
see on the front end of the site.

103
00:06:26,158 --> 00:06:29,944
The content block is empty, waiting for episode four.

104
00:06:30,744 --> 00:06:34,522
And one last thing, which is a genuine inconsistency.

105
00:06:34,522 --> 00:06:40,367
The requirements file that the template generated caps Django below six point one.

106
00:06:40,367 --> 00:06:45,001
But the Django pip actually installed is six point one point one.

107
00:06:45,001 --> 00:06:50,632
They disagree, because Wagtail's own package metadata asks only for Django five

108
00:06:50,632 --> 00:06:56,620
point two or newer with no upper limit, and pip follows the metadata, not this file.

109
00:06:56,620 --> 00:06:57,903
Nothing is broken.

110
00:06:57,903 --> 00:07:02,394
But that is exactly how your environment drifts away from mine.

111
00:07:03,194 --> 00:07:05,481
Five things to carry forward.

112
00:07:05,481 --> 00:07:09,739
Wagtail is about eleven Django apps in installed apps.

113
00:07:09,739 --> 00:07:13,051
The wagtail urls catch all must stay last.

114
00:07:13,051 --> 00:07:16,285
Your homepage came from a data migration,

115
00:07:16,285 --> 00:07:19,755
and its position is a treebeard path string.

116
00:07:19,755 --> 00:07:24,250
Templates resolve from app/model_name.html automatically.

117
00:07:24,250 --> 00:07:30,716
And two settings ship as placeholders: the dev secret key, and the admin base url.

118
00:07:31,516 --> 00:07:34,349
Next episode we finally change something,

119
00:07:34,349 --> 00:07:39,877
and the first thing to understand is the Page model that those six lines inherit

120
00:07:39,877 --> 00:07:40,222
from.

121
00:07:41,022 --> 00:07:47,254
Next episode, we finally change something.

122
00:07:47,254 --> 00:07:50,222
Thanks for watching.
